From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: FT: configure the PTK after association

hostapd patch 896 (sent to the hostap list 2026-11-04), B137: at FT
authentication wpa_ft_install_ptk() tries to configure the PTK before
the STA is associated; mac80211 refuses a pairwise key for an STA that
is not associated yet (-ENOENT), so every FT roam logs

  nl80211: kernel reports: key addition failed

at daemon.err, and the PTK is configured after association anyway by
the WPA_ASSOC_FT retry. The add_sta_ft callback now reports that case
and the early attempt is skipped; the PMF re-add case and EPP STAs are
unchanged.

On the fleet (-135) the error came in the same second as each
AP-STA-CONNECTED auth_alg=ft, 5 to 20 a day per AP. Tested on a W-118
(ath10k) with two FT-PSK BSSes: stock 6/6 roams with 6 errors, patched
6/6 roams with none, the station's CCMP key in place after each roam.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile     |  2 +-
 ...ssociation-with-full-AP-client-state.patch | 72 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
index 608ccdfbe88439af0ef078b11c10b3c0b938d423..0876c431af53b0f47ef0523804954f27a4ff8ad3 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=hostapd
-PKG_RELEASE:=17
+PKG_RELEASE:=18
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://w1.fi/hostap.git
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/896-FT-Configure-the-PTK-after-association-with-full-AP-client-state.patch b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/896-FT-Configure-the-PTK-after-association-with-full-AP-client-state.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..41f916ed8c1ac698318d01aa90e883923a793fa3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/896-FT-Configure-the-PTK-after-association-with-full-AP-client-state.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+From b6bc6569bd46049b51e51a2c4c8234b4e47648ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:08:43 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH] FT: Configure the PTK after association with full AP client
+ state
+
+At FT authentication, wpa_ft_install_ptk() tries to configure the PTK
+before the STA is associated. A driver with full AP client state
+(mac80211) refuses a pairwise key for an STA that is not associated
+yet (-ENOENT), so every FT authentication logs
+
+  nl80211: kernel reports: key addition failed
+
+as an error, and the PTK is configured after association anyway, by
+the retry for WPA_ASSOC_FT in wpa_auth_sm_event().
+
+Have the add_sta_ft callback report that case, and skip the attempt
+then. The PMF re-add case and EPP STAs are left as they are.
+
+Tested on OpenWrt with ath10k (mac80211) on an Arista W-118, two
+FT-PSK BSSs on one radio and a wpa_supplicant station roaming between
+them over the air: before, each of 6 roams logged the error; after,
+none in 6 roams, all completed, with the station's pairwise key in
+mac80211 after the roam and frames received with it.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+ src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c   | 7 +++++--
+ src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c | 8 ++++++++
+ 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+index e12f2ad..201c6d4 100644
+--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
++++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+@@ -2898,8 +2898,11 @@ void wpa_ft_install_ptk(struct wpa_state_machine *sm, int retry)
+ 		return;
+ 	}
+ 
+-	if (!retry)
+-		wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(sm->wpa_auth, sm->addr);
++	if (!retry && wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(sm->wpa_auth, sm->addr) == 1) {
++		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
++			   "FT: Configure the PTK to the driver after association");
++		return;
++	}
+ 
+ 	/* FIX: add STA entry to kernel/driver here? The set_key will fail
+ 	 * most likely without this.. At the moment, STA entry is added only
+diff --git a/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c b/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c
+index 9da2e6d..1336171 100644
+--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c
++++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_glue.c
+@@ -1332,6 +1332,14 @@ static int hostapd_wpa_auth_add_sta_ft(void *ctx, const u8 *sta_addr)
+ 		return ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta);
+ 	}
+ 
++	/* A driver with full AP client state takes a pairwise key only for
++	 * an associated STA (mac80211 refuses it with -ENOENT before that).
++	 * Have the PTK configured after association instead of trying here
++	 * and logging the driver's refusal at every FT authentication. */
++	if (FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
++	    !(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC) && !ap_sta_is_epp(sta))
++		return 1;
++
+ 	return 0;
+ }
+ 
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
